Implement user story SKY-002-b: Test suite for SkyscannerClient

## Story Description
Create src/skyscanner/client.test.ts with vitest tests that mock the global fetch — no real network calls. Cover URL/header construction, successful parsing, HTTP errors, missing-key errors, parse errors, and mock-mode behavior.

## Acceptance Criteria
- client.test.ts uses vitest with mocked fetch (vi.stubGlobal or equivalent) and afterEach fetch restoration — no real network calls in any test
- Test verifies searchFlights constructs the correct RapidAPI URL and headers (including the resolved API key)
- Test verifies a successful API response is parsed into a FlightResult[] matching the interface shape
- Test verifies HTTP 4xx/5xx responses cause searchFlights to reject with an Error containing the status code
- Test verifies missing or empty-string API key (constructor arg and RAPIDAPI_KEY env var combinations) causes the constructor to throw the missing-key Error
- Test verifies a malformed or missing-fields response body causes searchFlights to reject with a parse/validation Error
- Test verifies MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API='true' returns the fixture and global fetch is never invoked (spy/assert not called); test verifies non-'true' values (unset, empty, 'false', '1', 'TRUE') result in a real fetch call
- tsc --noEmit exits 0 and vitest run exits 0 with all tests passing


## Test Criteria (ground truth — written from actual source; overrides any conflicting AC)
- SkyscannerClient class exported from module
- Constructor signature: constructor({ apiKey }: { apiKey?: string } = {})
- Constructor throws Error with exact message: 'Skyscanner API key is missing. Provide it via the SkyscannerClient constructor or set RAPIDAPI_KEY in the environment.' when apiKey is empty string, undefined, and RAPIDAPI_KEY env var is also missing or empty
- searchFlights method signature: async searchFlights(params: SearchParams): Promise<FlightResult[]>
- SearchParams interface: { origin: string; destination: string; date: string; adults?: number }
- FlightResult interface: { price: number; currency: string; airline: string; departure: string; arrival: string; duration: number; stops: number }
- searchFlights validates params.origin is non-empty string, throws 'SearchParams.origin must be a non-empty string.' if invalid
- searchFlights validates params.destination is non-empty string, throws 'SearchParams.destination must be a non-empty string.' if invalid
- searchFlights validates params.date is non-empty string, throws 'SearchParams.date must be a non-empty string.' if invalid
- searchFlights validates params.adults is positive number when provided, throws 'SearchParams.adults must be a positive number when provided.' if invalid (adults <= 0 or not a number)
- MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API env check: process.env.MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API === 'true' (strict string equality, not truthy check)
- When MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API === 'true', searchFlights returns buildMockResults(params) without calling global fetch
- When MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API !== 'true', searchFlights constructs URL: 'https://skyscanner44.p.rapidapi.com/search?origin=<params.origin>&destination=<params.destination>&date=<params.date>' with optional '&adults=<params.adults>' if adults is provided
- Request headers include: 'x-rapidapi-key': this.#apiKey, 'x-rapidapi-host': 'skyscanner44.p.rapidapi.com', 'accept': 'application/json'
- HTTP error handling: throws Error with message 'Skyscanner API request failed with status <status>' or 'Skyscanner API request failed with status <status> <statusText>' when response.ok is false
- JSON parse error handling: throws Error with message starting 'Failed to parse Skyscanner API response JSON: ' followed by the error message
- Response validation: expects response body with results array at body.results, body.data, or body.flights
- Missing results array throws: 'Skyscanner response did not contain a results array.'
- Each flight result validated with validateFlight - throws specific errors like 'Flight result at index <n> has invalid price.' etc.
- buildMockResults returns 3 FlightResult objects with prices adjusted by adults count (199.99 + adults, 249.5 + adults, 312.0 + adults)
- Non-'true' MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API values (unset, empty string, 'false', '1', 'TRUE') result in real fetch call

